D. Dirichlet's half-row formula h(-p) = (sum_{0<a<p/2} (a/p)) / (2 - (2/p)), p = 3 mod 4, p > 3
==============================================================================
   [OK  ] formula exact for all 154 primes p = 3 (mod 4), 3 < p < 2000
   [OK  ] equivalently: half-row sum = h(-p) for p = 7 (mod 8) and = 3 h(-p) for p = 3 (mod 8)
   p = 3: half-row sum 1, 2 - (2/3) = 3, quotient 1/3 != h(-3) = 1: the hypothesis p > 3 is needed (extra units).
   p = 7: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..3} = 2 - 1 = 1 = 1 * h(-p) = 1 * 1
   p = 11: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..5} = 4 - 1 = 3 = 3 * h(-p) = 3 * 1
   p = 19: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..9} = 6 - 3 = 3 = 3 * h(-p) = 3 * 1
   p = 23: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..11} = 7 - 4 = 3 = 1 * h(-p) = 1 * 3
   p = 31: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..15} = 9 - 6 = 3 = 1 * h(-p) = 1 * 3
   p = 47: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..23} = 14 - 9 = 5 = 1 * h(-p) = 1 * 5
   p = 59: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..29} = 19 - 10 = 9 = 3 * h(-p) = 3 * 3
   p = 71: Paley tournament vertex 0, out - in into {1..35} = 21 - 14 = 7 = 1 * h(-p) = 1 * 7
   [OK  ] Paley reading: half-row sum = out-degree minus in-degree of vertex 0 into the first half (checked 8 primes)

